# shy-notes project rules

## Product

Floating always-on-top notepad that softly flees the cursor unless the user aims at the capture surface. Display name: `shy-notes`. Local-first; no accounts, network, telemetry, cloud sync, markdown, or multi-note in MVP.

## Stack

Tauri 2 + Rust + TypeScript (vanilla). Pure evasion logic lives in `crates/interaction-core` (no Tauri). Native adapter in `src-tauri`. Frontend only renders editor/feedback.

## Hard constraints

- English for all repo artifacts.
- No Cursor Cloud Agents / paid remote compute.
- Linux: X11 supported; Wayland best-effort (document limits; no fragile compositor hacks).
- Signing/notarization deferred; ship unsigned until Phase 8 credentials unlock.
- Default hotkey: Cmd+Shift+Space (macOS) / Ctrl+Shift+Space (Win/Linux).

## Architecture

Keep `interaction-core` free of I/O and window APIs. Physical pixels in the core; DPI conversion only in the native adapter. Prefer “do not move” when intent is ambiguous.

## Out of scope (MVP)

Rich text, AI, plugins, cloud, settings window, multiple notes, database.

## Process

Advance one phase at a time with a runnable app and documented gate. Do not accumulate unverified evasion features.
